# NO BINARIES IN THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# Everything here must be auditable from source.  That is why the pcode build
# is Python (gplbld/) rather than a shipped binary, and it is why the linked
# executables and libraries are not tracked, even though the install scripts
# used to deploy them straight from a clone.  Installing now means building.
#
# Do not add an exception to this for convenience.  If something needs to ship
# as a binary, it ships outside the repository - a release artefact, not a
# tracked file.
sdb_ai/sd64/bin/
!sdb_ai/sd64/bin/README
*.exe
*.dll
*.dll.a
*.a
*.o
*.so
*.lib
*.obj

# Compiler intermediates - regenerated by `make` in sdb_ai/sd64.
sdb_ai/sd64/gplobj/*.o

# Generated by the `terminfo` make target, which runs
# `sdtic -pterminfo terminfo.src` after clearing the directory.
# terminfo.src is the real source and stays tracked.
sdb_ai/sd64/terminfo/

# Build products of the vendored client library.
sdb_ai/sd64/gplsrc/sdclilib/*.dll
sdb_ai/sd64/gplsrc/sdclilib/*.dll.a
sdb_ai/sd64/gplsrc/sdclilib/*.exe

# 17 Aug 26 - localtest/ is where "make check-local" and "make
# check-select-probe" build and RUN their binaries, deliberately (see the long
# comment on check-local in that Makefile: the directory a test runs from
# decides which sdclilib.dll the loader finds).  The .exe files inside it were
# already covered by the global *.exe rule, but the results the probes write
# were not, so the directory goes as a whole.  gplbld/assert-current.ps1
# already skips it for the same reason - it is build output that happens to sit
# inside a watched source tree.
sdb_ai/sd64/gplsrc/sdclilib/localtest/

# Python bytecode.  gplbld/stage.py imports gplbld/bootstrap.py for the shared
# elevation test, so a build now leaves __pycache__ beside the scripts.  It is
# generated and it is binary, so it is not tracked - see the header.
__pycache__/

# Scratch output from the pcode build (gplbld/bbcmp.py, gplbld/pcode_bld.py).
sdb_ai/sd64/pcode_bld.log
sdb_ai/sd64/pass1
sdb_ai/sd64/pass2

# The staging tree gplbld/stage.py builds - "an install, laid out".  It is
# build output, like bin/ above: ~3,165 files including sd.exe and the MSYS2
# DLLs, so committing it would breach the no-binaries rule in CLAUDE.md.  The
# default location is ../../stage from sd64, which is the repository root.
stage/
